
========================================================================================================
1.  GATE ALGEBRA: the retention multiplier k(S) is DERIVED, not adopted
========================================================================================================

  Re G(omega) = 1/(1 + (omega/omega_c)^2)         [the paper's single-pole causal Debye relaxator]
  requirement Re G(omega_gal) >= S  <=>  omega_c >= k(S) * omega_gal
  sympy solve:  omega/omega_c at Re G = S  is  x*(S) = sqrt(1 - S)/sqrt(S)
                so  k(S) = 1/x*(S) = sqrt(S)/sqrt(1 - S) = sqrt(S/(1-S))
  k(0.90) = 3.000000   <- the paper's factor 3, reproduced from the gate, not assumed

   [PASS] k(S) satisfies the defining equation Re G(1/k) == S identically, and k(0.90) == 3 exactly
   [PASS] self-consistency: Re G(omega_gal, omega_c = k*omega_gal) == S for S = 0.90, 0.95, 0.99
   [PASS] inverse map S(k) = k^2/(1+k^2) round-trips k(S) for S in {0.90,0.93,0.95,0.99}

