========================================================================================================
3.  RETENTION SENSITIVITY -- what Re G >= 0.95 or 0.99 does to the lower edge
========================================================================================================

  Re G >= S is a TOLERANCE CHOICE, not a measurement: it is how much galactic-RAR degradation at the
  worst orbit the framework is willing to eat.  S = 0.90 means the gate is allowed to remove 10% of the
  MI boost at UGC05721's innermost point.  The lower edge scales as k(S) = sqrt(S/(1-S)), which is STEEP
  near 1: k(0.90) = 3, k(0.95) = 4.359, k(0.99) = 9.950.

  retention S        k(S)    lower edge   vs canon upper 2.211e-14   vs alt upper 1.831e-14
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  0.90             3.0000    1.7824e-14                     1.240x                   1.027x
  0.95             4.3589    2.5898e-14                     0.854x                   0.707x
  0.99             9.9499    5.9116e-14                     0.374x                   0.310x

  INVERSION -- the CRITICAL retention at which the window closes (lower edge == upper edge):
      canon:  k_crit = upper/MAX = 3.7214  ->  S_crit = 0.9327
      alt:    k_crit = upper/MAX = 3.0818  ->  S_crit = 0.9047

  So the canonical window exists only if the framework accepts >= 6.7% MI-boost loss at the
  fastest confirmed deep-MOND orbit, and the alt window only if it accepts >= 9.5%.  Demanding
  Re G >= 0.95 (a 5% RAR tolerance) closes BOTH footings; the alt footing closes at a retention demand
  of just 0.905, i.e. 0.5 percentage points above the adopted 0.90.
  With the beam guard (MAX -> 4.621e-15) the critical retentions relax to
      canon S_crit = 0.9581   alt S_crit = 0.9401
  -> the retention lever and the beam-guard lever are comparable in size and pull OPPOSITE ways.
  HONEST READING: the 0.90 tolerance is defensible (10% at one orbit sits inside the framework's own
  0.108 dex = 28% SPARC RAR scatter) but it is a CHOICE, and the window's width is a function of it.

   [PASS] Re G >= 0.95 closes both footings (k(0.95)*MAX exceeds both upper edges)
   [PASS] critical retentions are ordered and bracket the adopted 0.90 tightly (alt within 1 pp)

